 0}, "by_type": {}}, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 148, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "Done. Draft PR: https://github.com/kvndhrty/quorum/pull/107 (branch `quorum/8v3yk0`, one commit, rebased onto `origin/main` after #105).\n\n**What landed**\n\n`forge.py` is new and is now the only module that invokes a forge CLI. It holds three entry points across two contracts: `run_json` (soft, behind `ci.pr_state`), `auth_status` (soft, for `doctor`), and `issue_view` (loud, for `task add --issue`). All three go through one `subprocess.run` and ask `cli_name(home)` for the binary — that function is the single named seam for #51's `gh | glab | none` switch, which I left untouched. `ci.py` keeps the digest half over it and `[ci]`'s two switches gate both halves; `doctor` now borrows `forge.auth_status`. No write path to a forge.\n\n`task add --issue <number|url>` composes `<title>\\n\\n<body>\\n\\n(<url>)`, appends any prompt given alongside, and records `issue_url` (written once at `add`, never re-probed). `tasks.issue_ref` is the one renderer of `#62`, used by the CLI listing's new `issue` column (dropped when empty), the TUI and web tables, and the digest's active and recently-finished task lines; `task show` prints the full URL; the preamble's new `{issue}` slot tells the harness which issue it is working from, with the same \"edited preamble without the placeholder\" append fallback `{perpetual}` has.\n\nFailures are loud, as asked: bad reference (refused before any subprocess), no gh, unauthenticated, unknown issue, timeout, garbage, or a reply missing url/title each raise `ForgeError` with the fix named, and nothing is queued.\n\n**Verification** — `uv run pytest`: 665 passed, 2 skipped; `uv run ruff check .` clean. `tests/bin/fake_gh.py` grew `issue view` plus a `noissue` mode, and the gh fixtures moved to `conftest.py` so `test_forge.py` and `test_ci.py` drive the same fake. I also ran the real path by hand against this repo with real `gh` (success, unknown issue, bad reference) in a throwaway home. Docs updated in the same commit: `docs/architecture.md` (\"From an issue\", \"The forge seam\"), `docs/guide.md`, CLAUDE.md's gh rule, one CHANGELOG bullet under Added.\n\nTwo notes on your heads-up: I dropped the `SUPERSEDED_PROMPT_HASHES` entry, so `home.py` is not in the commit at all — the rebase conflict took main's side. And the CHANGELOG's existing \"Upgrading\" item 1 still says prompt copies are \"recognized by hash\", which #105 made stale; I only added the `{issue}` mention there and left that phrasing to you rather than editing another PR's note.", "ttft_ms": 1867, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 1453811, "uuid": "3b74f541-5ff8-49f1-a801-413e51a8168a", "ttft_stream_ms": 1670, "time_to_request_ms": 18, "queued_turn_count": 0}}
